## Universal Performance Checklist (always apply)
- **N+1 Queries**: DB calls inside a loop — each iteration hits the DB instead of a single batch.
- **Missing Pagination**: Queries fetching unbounded result sets that will grow over time.
- **Blocking I/O in async context**: Blocking call (file read, HTTP call, DB query) made without async handling in an async framework.
- **Redundant computation**: Same value computed multiple times per request when it could be computed once.
- **Memory leaks**: Event listeners, timers, subscriptions, or large objects created but never released.
- **Unbounded data structures**: Lists, maps, or queues accumulated without a size cap.
- **Inefficient serialization**: Large objects serialized/deserialized repeatedly in hot paths.
- **Missing indexes**: New query patterns filtering or sorting on columns that likely lack a DB index.
- **Cache misuse**: Results fetched on every request that should be cached; or stale results from missing invalidation.
- **Algorithm complexity**: New loops or data operations introducing O(n²) or worse behavior.
- **Eager loading of large data**: Fetching an entire resource when only a subset of fields is needed.
- **Connection not pooled**: New DB or HTTP clients created per-request instead of from a shared pool.

